  "style": [
    "Address the user informally with “du” (lowercase), as Notion and Linear do in German.",
    "Buttons and menu items use the infinitive, without a final full stop (e.g. “Notiz erstellen”, “Einstellungen öffnen”).",
    "Use German quotation marks „…“ and keep compound nouns readable; hyphenate English loanwords in compounds (e.g. “Markdown-Datei”).",
    "Keep UI text short; German runs long, so prefer the shorter of two natural options.",
    "Keep placeholders such as {count} or {title} exactly as written, and reorder them freely to fit the target language's word order.",
    "Keep keyboard symbols and key names (⌘ ⌥ ⇧ ⌃ ↵ Esc Tab Enter Space) and shortcut letters unchanged.",
    "Keep the source's ellipsis “…” and the middle dot “·” as they are.",
    "Translate meaning, not words; prefer the wording established apps on this platform use (Finder, Notes, Obsidian, Notion, Linear)."
